{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.1-4", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.1-4"}, "paraphrase": "Brahmā (Hiraṇyagarbha) asks Maheśvara about kaivalya; he is taught the path of the siddhas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:brahma", "tch:siva"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.1-4"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.1-4 located in the e-text; the passage matches the paraphrase.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.12-14", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.12-14"}, "paraphrase": "Some say knowledge alone suffices; it does not bring perfection. Knowledge without yoga cannot liberate; yoga without knowledge is incapable; the seeker should practise both.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:yoga-jnana-samuccaya"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "cross_refs": ["tea:yogatattva-upanisad:14-15"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.12-14"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.12-14 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'tasmāddoṣavināśārtha-mupāyaṃ kathayāmi te | jñānaṃ kecidvadantyatra kevalaṃ tanna siddhaye || 12 ||yogahīnaṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.129-138", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.129-138"}, "paraphrase": "Mantra, laya, haṭha and rāja are four stages of one great yoga: mantra-yoga is the natural haṃsa repetition reversed as so'ham; haṭha the union of ha (sun) and ṭha (moon); laya the union of the knower of the field and the supreme; rāja the union of rajas and retas.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-yogas", "cpt:hamsa"], "paths": ["pth:yogatattva-four-yogas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.129-138"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.129-138 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'kathitantu tava prītyā hyetadabhyāsalakṣaṇam | mantro layo haṭho rājayogo'ntarbhūmikāḥkramāt || 129 || eka…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.140-144", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.140-144"}, "paraphrase": "Two ways: the monkey's (gradual, completed in one body) and the crow's (the body perishes, he is reborn, meets a siddha guru and gains the fruit quickly).", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:monkey-and-crow-paths"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.140-144"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.140-144 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'ekenaiva śarīreṇa yogābhyāsācchanaiḥśanaiḥ | cirātsamprāpyate muktirmarkaṭakramaeva saḥ || 140 || yogasiddhiṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.151-160", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.151-160"}, "paraphrase": "Powers are of two kinds: contrived (from mercury, herbs, rites, mantras — impermanent and weak) and uncontrived (arising spontaneously, permanent, in those free of vāsanās); they are to be kept secret, like tīrthas seen on the way. As goldsmiths test gold, the siddha is known by his powers; one without powers is still bound.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhis-in-yoga-upanisads"], "disputes": ["dsp:siddhis-sign-or-obstacle"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.151-160"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.151-160 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'siddhānityā mahāvīryā icchārūpāḥ svayogajāḥ | cirakālātprajāyante vāsanārahi-teṣu ca || 155 || tāstu gopyā…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.161-163", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.161-163"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation is not the falling of the body; the yogin's body becomes Brahman like salt dissolved in water.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "body-layers"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.161-163"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.161-163 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'ajarāmarapiṇḍo yojīvanmuktaḥ sa eva hi | paśukukkuṭakīṭādhyā mṛtiṃ samprāpnuvanti vai || 161 ||teṣāṃ kiṃ…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.165-178", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.165-178"}, "paraphrase": "The body is Śiva's temple: ten doors, channels and winds; four seats (pīṭha) — Kāmarūpa at the mūlādhāra, Pūrṇagiri at the heart, Jālandhara at the throat, Uḍyāna between the brows.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:body-as-temple", "cpt:cakras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.165-178"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.165-178 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: '172 || dvādaśārammahācakraṃ hṛdaye cāpyanāhatam | tadetatpūrṇagiryākhyaṃ pīṭhaṃ kamalasambhava || 173…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.24-26", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.24-26"}, "paraphrase": "Even the knower needs the yoga of the body; bodies are unripe (apakva) or ripened (pakva) by the fire of yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["body-layers", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.24-26"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.24-26 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'jñānaṃ cedīdṛśaṃ jñātamajñānaṃ kīdṛśaṃ punaḥ | jñānaniṣṭho vira-kto'pi dharmajño vijitendriyaḥ || 24 || vinā…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.40-53", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.40-53"}, "paraphrase": "The yogin's body, burnt by the fire of yoga, is unseen even by gods; other knowers are 'lumps of flesh' reborn again, who meet a siddha and become yogins; knowledge comes from yoga in one birth; there is no path beyond yoga.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:ripe-and-unripe-body"], "disputes": ["dsp:yoga-or-knowledge-for-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.40-53"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.40-53 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'mahābhūtāni tattvāni saṃhṛtāni krameṇa ca | saptadhātumayo deho dagdho yogā gninā śanaiḥ || 40 || devairapi…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.54-55", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.54-55"}, "paraphrase": "Merely thinking 'I am liberated' does not liberate at once.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.54-55"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.54-55 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'pravicārya ciraṃ jñānaṃ mukto'hamiti manyate | kimasau mana-nādeva mukto bhavati tatkṣaṇāt || 54 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.59-66", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.59-66"}, "paraphrase": "Mind is tied to prāṇa like a bird tied by a string; the only means is prāṇa. Partial knowledge brings great suffering; it is like crossing the ocean in an unbaked pot.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "practice"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.59-66"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.59-66 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'cittaṃ prāṇena sambaddhaṃ sarvajīveṣu saṃsthi-tam | rajjvā yadvatsusambaddhaḥ pakṣī tadvadidaṃ manaḥ || 59 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:1.68-69", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.68-69"}, "paraphrase": "Yoga is the union of apāna and prāṇa, of rajas and retas, of sun and moon, of jīvātman and paramātman.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:bindu"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 1.68-69"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.68-69 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'yo'pānaprāṇayoraikyaṃ svarajoretasostathā | sūryācandramasoryogo jīvātmapara-mātmanoḥ || 68 || evaṃ tu…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:2.14-19", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.14-19"}, "paraphrase": "Brahman has three bodies — gross (Vairāja), subtle (Hiraṇyagarbha, nāda) and supreme (being-consciousness-bliss); signs of the subtle are a lamp-flame, the moon, fireflies, lightning and stars.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 2.14-19"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 2.14-19 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'gurūpadeśa-mārgeṇa sahasaiva prakāśate | sthūlaṃ sūkṣmaṃ paraṃ ceti trividhaṃ brahmaṇo vapuḥ|| 14 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:2.2-3", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.2-3"}, "paraphrase": "This should be taught only to one who has served for twelve years.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:secrecy-and-eligibility"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 2.2-3"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 2.2-3 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'śṛṇu brahmanpravakṣyāmi gopanīyaṃ prayatnataḥ | dvādaśābdantu śuśrūṣāṃ yaḥ kuryādapramādataḥ || 2 || tasmai…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
