{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.17-18", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.17-18"}, "paraphrase": "Of the 72,000 doors only the suṣumnā — the power of Śambhu — is useful; the others are useless.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:nadis"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 6.17-18"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6.17-18 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'kṛtvā tu caindavasthāne ghrāṇarandhre nirodhayet | dvisaptatisahasrāṇināḍīdvārāṇi pañjare || 17 || suṣumnā…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.26-28", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.26-28"}, "paraphrase": "Liberation comes if the guru himself is pleased; restraining the breath at the ādhāra the body trembles and the yogin dances.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 6.26-28"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6.26-28 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'ādhāracakra-mahasā vidyutpuñjasamaprabhā | tadā muktirna sandeho yadi tuṣṭaḥ svayaṃ guruḥ || 26…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.35-46", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.35-46"}, "paraphrase": "The suṣumnā is praised as the supreme tīrtha — greater than Gaṅgā, Maṇikarṇikā, Śrīśaila, Vārāṇasī and Kedāra; a thousand horse-sacrifices are not worth a sixteenth of it; it is the supreme japa and meditation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:inner-tirthas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 6.35-46"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6.35-46 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'suṣumnāyāṃ yadā haṃsastvadha ūrdhvampradhāvati | suṣumnāyāṃ yadā prāṇaṃ bhrāmayedyo nirantaram || 35 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.58-61", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.58-61"}, "paraphrase": "A moving mind is saṃsāra, a still mind liberation; the unmanī state is beyond merit and sin.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 6.58-61"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6.58-61 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'citte calati saṃsāroniścalaṃ mokṣa ucyate | tasmāccittaṃ sthirīkuryātprajñayā parayā vidhe || 58 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.62-66", "source": "src:yogasikha-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "6.62-66"}, "paraphrase": "The mind looking at the mind: the ten signs (pratyaya) — bindu, nāda, kalā, light, sun, moon, pole-star, star, the peaceful and what is beyond — make him lord of yogins.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogasikha-upanisad 6.62-66"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 6.62-66 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'manasāmana ālokya vṛttiśūnyaṃ yadā bhavet | tataḥ paraṃ parabrahma dṛśyate ca sudurlabham|| 62 || manasā mana…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
